  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Anticipate cooler temperatures and periods of valley rain and\n   mountain snow through the weekend.\n\n\nNorthern Rockies is currently under westerly flow aloft as a low\npressure system is dropping southward along the Pacific\nNorthwest coast. This system is ushering in a fetch of moisture\ncausing numerous showers across the region. Snow levels appear to\nbe hovering around 4000 feet this morning with snow sticking to\nroadways above 5000 feet. Lolo, Lost Trail and Marias passes will\nbe dealing with snow covered roads through mid to late morning.  \n\nThe low pressure system will continue to dig along the coast\ncausing the upper level flow to become more southwesterly over the\nNorthern Rockies. This flow pattern will keep periods of showers\nover the region, but snow levels will be rising up to 6000 feet. \n\nThe low pressure system is anticipated to track across the\nNorthern Rockies Saturday night into Sunday causing cooler\ntemperatures and widespread precipitation once again. \n\nThe long term models are indicating a ridge of high pressure\nbuilding over the region by mid next week causing a warming and\ndrying trend especially in the higher terrain. The valleys will be\ndealing with inversions potentially causing fog under this pattern\nfor the first week of November.",
